# Fix View Report and Verify Auth

The "View Report" feature in the Live Scan Registry is failing because the scan details page (`/scans/[id]`) does not include the authentication token in its API requests, causing the backend (which is secured) to reject the request. Additionally, the page uses a hardcoded localhost URL instead of the proxied `/api` route.

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE]
> No breaking changes. This is a fix for existing non-functional code.

## Proposed Changes

### UI
#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/ui/app/scans/[id]/page.tsx)
- Import `useAuth` hook.
- Add authentication check (redirect to `/login` if not logged in).
- Update `fetch` call to use `/api/scans/${id}` instead of `http://localhost:8080...`.
- Add `Authorization: Bearer ${token}` header to the `fetch` request.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1.  **Code Review**: Verify that `ui/app/scans/[id]/page.tsx` logic matches [ui/app/scans/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/ui/app/scans/page.tsx) in terms of authentication handling.
2.  **User Verification**: Ask the user to click "View Report" again. It should now load the report details instead of showing an error or loading indefinitely.

### Automated Tests
- None available for UI components in the current environment. Relying on code correctness and consistency with working pages.
